  "details": "I think I did post it before but I worded it differently kind of. I thought vrchat would be the coolest place to read books inside. I have books on c# and java script and learning all kinds of cool stuff I read. I think it would be really cool if you could open up a book and upload a pdf from your computer and have a virtual reality book inside vrchat that you could sit down at a vr table and flip through the pages and read just like a normal book in real life. Maybe it could be client sided and have fake words that other people would see or something and only I could read the words if that would make it easier or something. Maybe even in game media players as well. a book that doubled as a media player that could also play videos or something but only on the user side maybe both sides if its possible. Maybe a media player that looked like a book that played music and had moving pictures as videos that only I could hear unless someone clicks it and chooses to hear it. The moving pictures similar to in harry potter pretty much for movies or video files that get uploaded from your pc. Maybe it could start off as a small hand held book but you could throw it in front of you and it could grow into a larger one. Maybe not I dont know maybe it would be lame or ruin the game or something. Summoning screens though that could play videos, music, pdfs, or websites might be cool. Maybe if the summoned screens had different layouts instead of a book that way its different for everyone.  ",
